```
  ═══ COPY ON INPUT + COPY ON OUTPUT ═══

  class Account {
     private final List<Transaction> txns;

     Account(List<Transaction> seed) {
        this.txns = new ArrayList<>(seed);   // DEFENSIVE copy IN
     }                                        // caller's list can't leak in

     List<Transaction> getTransactions() {
        return List.copyOf(txns);            // immutable copy OUT
     }                                        // caller.add() → UnsupportedOp
     void post(Transaction t){ txns.add(t); } // ONLY controlled mutation
  }

  BAD:  return txns;            // live reference escapes → aliasing bug
  GOOD: return List.copyOf(txns);

  Also deep-copy if elements themselves are mutable (Date, arrays).

  SOLID: Encapsulation / information hiding — class owns its invariants.
  Pattern: Immutable view at the boundary; prevents representation exposure.
```
